  "priorExpiration": "2009-11-11",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5001.02 Exceptions. These rules shall not apply to:\n\n(a) The transportation of display fireworks that are under the jurisdiction of the Hazardous Materials Regulation Board of the U.S. Department of Transportation (DOT); and\n\n(b) The transportation and use of military display fireworks by federal and state military departments or federal, state and municipal police departments while in the performance of their duties.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5000) #6055, eff 7-1-95; ss by #7481, eff 4-25-01, EXPIRED: 4-25-09\n\nNew. #9471, INTERIM, eff 5-15-09, EXPIRED: 11-11-09\n\nNew. #9765-A, eff 8-2-10; ss by #12738, eff 4-30-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5000.html"
